# Offline testing

All of these run with no network (stdlib only unless noted).

## Python suites (run from repo root)

```bash
python3 actions/scrape-hearings/test_scrape_hearings.py
python3 actions/scrape-elections/test_scrape_elections.py
python3 scripts/test_build_people_roster.py
python3 scripts/test_dashboard_tags.py
python3 actions/scrape-maps/main.py --self-test
```

Or everything at once: `just test` (root `justfile`).

## Rust CLI (`actions/govbot/`, needs Rust + `just`)

```bash
just setup   # toolchain + cargo-insta, first time only
just test    # snapshot tests (insta)
just review  # review snapshot diffs before accepting
just check   # fmt --check + clippy -D warnings + tests
just govbot logs --repos il --limit 10   # dev run, repo-local data dir
just mocks wy gu                          # refresh mock data (needs network)
```

## Mock data

`actions/govbot/mocks/govbot_data/repos/` holds Wyoming + Guam samples:
`govbot logs --govbot-dir ./actions/govbot/mocks/govbot_data`.
Note: mock bill subtrees use `country:us/...` paths, which Windows checkouts
exclude — mock-based runs need Linux/macOS (or CI).

## Rule

If your change alters output, update or add snapshots. Never weaken a test to
fit code; fix the code. Keep changes minimal and focused.
